|term[descriptor]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss What an act supplies to narrow candidates; comes in exactly two kinds, split by what connects it to the referent.
  |designation descriptor
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-descriptors
    :anchor descriptor-kinds
    :projection paraphrase
    Descriptors come in two kinds, distinguished by what connects the descriptor to its referent — an agreement, or a fact.
  |formal
    :notation <latex:Descriptor = Designator \sqcup Description>
    :reading The two kinds partition the space; the partition axis is the binding (agreement vs recomputed fact).
  |set-rel :kind partitions :into [@designator @description]
  |rel :kind part-of :to @reference-act
  |invariant
    Kind is determined by whether anyone maintains the binding, never by the spelling (D8).
